  "audio": "011.once-you-see.mp3",
  "paragraph": 11,
  "text": "Once you see that mechanism, tool design suddenly matters a lot more than people expect. A common rookie mistake is dumping sixty overlapping tools into the harness, or wiring up five MCP servers that inject seventy verbose JSON schemas before turn one. That burns tens of thousands of prompt tokens before the agent reads a single line of code, while actively confusing tool selection. In practice, a small set of sharp, composable primitives like read, edit, search, and shell consistently beats bloated tool catalogs.",
